hello i'm greg sadler and i would like  to invite you to stoicon 2022  which will be taking place on saturday  october 29th it's an online conference  that everybody can participate in either  through the zoom that we'll be setting  up or through the modern stoicism  youtube channel if you're not familiar  with stoicon it is the  world's largest gathering of stoics and  this is the tenth year of stoicons and  i'll also add of stoic week which will  be going on roughly the same time the  stoicons early on took place in london  and new york city  toronto athens in greece and then with  covid they went online and we realized  that we could make it so much more  accessible to so many more people by  keeping it as an online conference and  that is precisely what we are doing for  the third time this year so we've got a  lot of great talks and workshops lined  up i just want to go through the  schedule a little bit i won't be saying  which times there you can click the link  that's below and find out all of that so  we'll begin with some opening remarks by  myself and some of the other conference  organizers andy shaka philianov and by  john sellers joining us as well  and then we're going to have a talk by  my friend and colleague peter stan kuich  why reformed stoicism something he's  proposing  then we'll have uh stoicism around the  world panel which is going to be  particularly  interesting with uh representatives of  stoic communities all over uh henry  manampiring from indonesia aldo dinucci  from brazil kelly andreas rodriguez from  spain  sasha roehter  from  germany and logan wallingdom from  norway with greg lopez moderating then  we'll have another talk coming up by  brittany palette from pre-rational  instinct to rational care  and then we'll have the big plenary talk  we're really happy this year to have  christopher gill one of the founders of  modern stoicism stoic week stoicon still  heavily involved in all of what's going  on and he is going to be giving a talk  called care of oneself others in our  world can stoicism help us to hold these  together  then  after a short break we will have a  personal  storytelling workshop by catherine  cormilas called becoming hercules  finding your superpowers understanding  your role in life and choosing your life  path very interactive and should be a  lot of fun  following that we are going to have  lightning round talks that are  contributed by anybody who wants to do a  short  two to five minute pre-recorded talk to  send in to us we'll stitch them all  together and that will as always be very  stimulating then we'll have another talk  by rob coulter  theory practice and pepsis if you don't  know rob coulter he and massimo  pigliucci have a great stoic podcast  actually philosophy is a way of life  podcast that you might find interesting  and then we will be finishing up with  another panel and this one will be  authors of and editors actually too  of recent books on stoicism so we'll  have duff lambros donald robertson kevin  vost david fideller  nancy sherman and my co-editor of  stoicism today selected essays volumes  three and four leia goldrick will be  participating as well harold covley will  be moderating that and then after that  we're gonna it's the sort of like big  question mark we're gonna have an after  party and casual conversation with  people who want to hang around online  and do that so it's an entire day  of great talks workshops panels you can  pop in for as much as you'd like  it's going there's going to be breaks in  between one of the  really the only complaint that we had  last year where the breaks were not  quite as long as people would like and  the reason was because the conference  was so good  nobody wanted to step away from it for  even a minute so it's going to be just  as good this year i hope that you can  join us for this really  stimulating event it is sort of a  celebration of all things stoics with  great speakers and panels all sorts of  thought-provoking things and practices  and principles that you can take home  and start applying in your life today so  i hope that you'll join us put it on  your calendar october 29th and i'll  hopefully see you there i'm gonna be the  mc  so if you are there you'll see a little  bit of me and lots and lots of all of  these other  great speakers and scholars and  contributors and coaches having to do  with  stoicism and ancient philosophy in the  modern world
 

